      <div type="clause" n="3.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 3.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ eac swilce cynges hordera oððe ure gerefena, swilc ðære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.13"/> ðeofa gewita wære ðe staledon, beo he be ðam ilcan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ eac swylc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.20"/> cynges hordere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.21"/> oððe ure gerefena, hwylc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.22"/> ðara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.23"/> ðeofa gewita wære ðe staledon, beo be ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.3"/> ilcan.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.14"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ eac swylce cyninges hordra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.2"/> oððe ure gerefena, hwelc þæra þe þeofa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.7"/> gewita wære þe staledon, beo be þæm ylcan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>Et quicumque hordera<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.19"/> regis uel prepositus, qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.20-2"/> furi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.21-2"/> consentaneus erit, similiter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.22-2"/> reus habebitur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/> (simili sententie subiacebit).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="130" ed="#attenborough"/>⁊ eac swilce cynges hordera<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_3-2.attnote.fn.2"/> oððe ure gerefena hwylc<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_3-2.attnote.fn.3"/> ðara ðeofa gewita wære ðe staledon, beo he be ðam ilcan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>Und auch jeder Königskämmerer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_3-2.lnote.de.1"/> oder [jeder] unserer Vögte, welcher Mitwisser jener Diebe, die stehlen, wäre, sei unter demselben [Strafgesetz].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And likewise any king's treasurer or [any] of our reeves who was an accessory of those thieves who stole, let him be under the same [penal law].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="131" ed="#attenborough"/>And in like manner also, any of the royal treasurers<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_3-2.attnote.n.1"/> or [any] of our reeves who have been accessories of thieves, who have been guilty of stealing, shall suffer the same [penalty].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="419" ed="#whitelock"/>And likewise any of the king’s treasurers or of our reeves, who has been an accessory of thieves who have committed theft, is to be liable to the same.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="383"><ref target="clause:Iudex_Iudex-1">Iudex</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">swylce <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">swylce Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ra <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ra Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">h <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. auf Rasur B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">h on an erasure in the 16th cent. B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðe ðæra <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðe ðæra Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">yl. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">yl. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">und</hi> e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ and e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Or;</hi> orderra <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> hordea <hi rend="italic">TM;</hi> ordea <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Or; orderra K; hordea TM; ordea Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.21-2" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.22-2" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> s. r. h. [habeatur <hi rend="italic">Or</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> s. se. sub. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only s. r. h. [habeatur Or] Lond; only s. se. sub. the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond; fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þeofu</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þeofu</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Wergeld 30 k; Schatzmeister 1: nicht des Reiches, sondern lokaler Finanz; Poole <hi rend="italic">Exchequer</hi> 21. Das Wort, von Q mehrfach unübersetzt gelassen, bezeichnet auch den Wirtschaftsverwalter geistlichen Stifts, von Ælfric ‘Kellermeister’ übersetzt; Toller. — Die Königsurk. a. 892 Bi 567 mit <hi rend="italic">cellerarius, thesaurarius, pincerna</hi> ist unecht. K. Eadreds Testament bedenkt hinter Truchsess, Kämmerer, Schenk den ‘Priester bei meinen Reliquien’; a. 955 Bi 912. Über Eadwards III. Schatzmeister s. Round <hi rend="italic">EHR</hi> 1904, 92</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Wergeld 30 k; Schatzmeister 1: not of the realm but of local finance; Poole <hi rend="italic">Exchequer</hi> 21. The word, which Q several times leaves untranslated, also denotes the steward of a religious foundation, and is translated ‘cellarer’ by Ælfric; Toller. — The royal charter a. 892 Bi 567 with <hi rend="italic">cellerarius, thesaurarius, pincerna</hi> is spurious. King Eadred’s will remembers, after the seneschal, chamberlain and butler, the ‘priest in charge of my relics’; a. 955 Bi 912. On Eadward III’s treasurer see Round <hi rend="italic">EHR</hi> 1904, 92</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e</hi>. financial officials of the king in the various districts (Liebermann); cf. III Edm. cap. 5.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>hordera</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hordere</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_3-2.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>hwylc</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hwylc</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">hwelc</hi>. So.</seg></note>
      </div>
